{"timestamp":1789798170,"method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"01a0b847-713d-7ca1-9b4a-ec79a1525fe0","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"The user wants me to compute 7^8432 mod 5557 using modular exponentiation, showing each squaring step briefly, then stating the final remainder on its own line. They explicitly said not to use any tools.\n\nLet me compute this by hand. 8432 in binary: let me find the binary representation.\n\n8432 / 2 = 4216 r 0\n4216 / 2 = 2108 r 0\n2108 / 2 = 1054 r 0\n1054 / 2 = 527 r 0\n527 / 2 = 263 r 1\n263 / 2 = 131 r 1\n131 / 2 = 65 r 1\n65 / 2 = 32 r 1\n32 / 2 = 16 r 0\n16 / 2 = 8 r 0\n8 / 2 = 4 r 0\n4 / 2 = 2 r 0\n2 / 2 = 1 r 0\n1 / 2 = 0 r 1\n\nSo reading from bottom to top: 10000011110000\n\nLet me verify: 8432 = 8192 + 240 = 8192 + 128 + 64 + 32 + 16 = 8192 + 240. Wait 128+64+32+16 = 240. Yes. 8192+240 = 8432. Good.\n\nSo binary: 10000011110000\n\nLet me write it out: 8432 = 2^13 + 2^7 + 2^6 + 2^5 + 2^4\n8192 + 128 + 64 + 32 + 16 = 8432. Yes!\n\nSo bits set at positions 4, 5, 6, 7, 13 (0-indexed).\n\nNow modular exponentiation by squaring. I'll compute 7^(2^k) mod 5557 for k = 0, 1, 2, ...\n\nm = 5557.\n\nLet me factor 5557 to potentially use CRT. 5557... let me check. 5557 / 7 = 793.86... no. 5557 / 11 = 505.2 no. /13 = 427.5 no. /17 = 326.9 no. /19 = 292.5 no. /23 = 241.6 no. /29 = 191.6 no. /31 = 179.3 no. /37 = 150.2 no. /41 = 135.5 no. /43 = 129.2 no. /47 = 118.2 no. /53 = 104.8 no. /59 = 94.2 no. /61 = 91.1 no. /67 = 82.9 no. /71 = 78.3 no. /73 = 76.1 no. sqrt(5557) ≈ 74.5. So check primes up to 74.\n\nLet me redo: 5557. Is it prime? Let me check divisibility.\n5557 odd, not div by 2. Sum digits 5+5+5+7=22, not div by 3. Not div by 5. 5557/7: 7*793=5551, 7*794=5558, so no. /11: 11*505=5555, no. /13: 13*427=5551, 13*428=5564, no. /17: 17*326=5542, 17*327=5559, no. /19: 19*292=5548, 19*293=5567, no. /23: 23*241=5543, 23*242=5566, no. /29: 29*191=5539, 29*192=5568, no. /31: 31*179=5549, 31*180=5580, no. /37: 37*150=5550, 37*151=5587, no. /41: 41*135=5535, 41*136=5576, no. /43: 43*129=5547, 43*130=5590, no. /47: 47*118=5546, 47*119=5593, no. /53: 53*104=5512, 53*105=5565, no. /59: 59*94=5546, 59*95=5605, no. /61: 61*91=5551, 61*92=5612, no. /67: 67*82=5494, 67*83=5561, no. /71: 71*78=5538, 71*79=5609, no. /73: 73*76=5548, 73*77=5621, no.\n\nSo 5557 is prime! Good, that means I can use Fermat's little theorem: 7^(5556) ≡ 1 mod 5557.\n\n8432 mod 5556: 8432 - 5556 = 2876. So 7^8432 ≡ 7^2876 mod 5557.\n\nNow 2876 in binary: \n2876 / 2 = 1438 r 0\n1438 / 2 = 719 r 0\n719 / 2 = 359 r 1\n359 / 2 = 179 r 1\n179 / 2 = 89 r 1\n89 / 2 = 44 r 1\n44 / 2 = 22 r 0\n22 / 2 = 11 r 0\n11 / 2 = 5 r 1\n5 / 2 = 2 r 1\n2 / 2 = 1 r 0\n1 / 2 = 0 r 1\n\nSo 2876 = 101100111100 in binary. Let me verify: 2048 + 512 + 256 + 32 + 16 + 8 + 4 = 2048+512=2560, +256=2816, +32=2848, +16=2864, +8=2872, +4=2876. Yes!\n\nSo 2876 = 2^11 + 2^9 + 2^8 + 2^5 + 2^4 + 2^3 + 2^2.\nBits set at positions 2, 3, 4, 5, 8, 9, 11.\n\nThis is still a lot of squaring (12 squarings to get to 2^11). Let me just do the squaring. Actually, maybe I can reduce further? No, Fermat gives 7^5556 ≡ 1, so 7^8432 = 7^(5556+2876) = 7^2876. That's the reduction.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. Maybe it's easier to just do modular exponentiation directly on 8432 with squaring up to 2^13. Either way I need to square up to 2^13 or up to 2^11. Using Fermat saves me 2 squarings. Let me use it: compute 7^2876 mod 5557.\n\nLet me compute the squares. m = 5557.\n\na0 = 7 (this is 7^(2^0))\na1 = 7^2 mod 5557 = 49\na2 = 49^2 mod 5557 = 2401\na3 = 2401^2 mod 5557 = 5,764,801 mod 5557.\n\nLet me compute 2401^2 = 5,764,801. \n5557 * 1000 = 5,557,000. 5,764,801 - 5,557,000 = 207,801.\n5557 * 37 = 205,609. 207,801 - 205,609 = 2,192.\nSo a3 = 2192. Check 5557*37: 5557*30=166710, 5557*7=38899, total 205609. Yes. 207801-205609=2192. Good.\n\na4 = 2192^2 mod 5557. 2192^2 = 4,804,864.\n5557 * 864 = ? 5557*800=4,445,600. 5557*64=355,648. Total 4,801,248. 4,804,864 - 4,801,248 = 3,616.\nSo a4 = 3616. Let me double check 5557*64: 5557*60=333420, 5557*4=22228, total 355648. 4445600+355648=4801248. 4804864-4801248=3616. Good.\n\na5 = 3616^2 mod 5557. 3616^2 = 13,075,456.\nLet me reduce. 5557 * 2000 = 11,114,000. 13,075,456 - 11,114,000 = 1,961,456.\n5557 * 353 = ? 5557*350 = 1,944,950. 5557*3 = 16,671. Total 1,961,621. That's slightly more than 1,961,456. So 353 too big. Try 352: 1,961,621 - 5,557 = 1,956,064. 1,961,456 - 1,956,064 = 5,392. 5392 < 5557. So a5 = 5392.\nLet me verify: 5557*2352 = 5557*2000 + 5557*352 = 11,114,000 + 1,956,064 = 13,070,064. 13,075,456 - 13,070,064 = 5,392. Good. a5 = 5392.\n\na6 = 5392^2 mod 5557. Note 5392 = 5557 - 165, so 5392 ≡ -165 mod 5557. (-165)^2 = 27225. 27225 mod 5557: 5557*4 = 22228. 27225 - 22228 = 4997. So a6 = 4997.\nCheck: 5392^2 = 29,073,664. And (-165)^2 = 27225, 27225 - 22228 = 4997. And 29073664 mod 5557 should be 4997. Let me verify 5392 = 5557-165, yes 5557-165=5392. Good. a6 = 4997.\n\na7 = 4997^2 mod 5557. 4997 = 5557 - 560, so ≡ -560. (-560)^2 = 313,600. 313,600 mod 5557: 5557*56 = 311,192. 313,600 - 311,192 = 2,408. So a7 = 2408.\nCheck 5557*56: 5557*50=277850, 5557*6=33342, total 311192. 313600-311192=2408. Good. a7 = 2408.\n\na8 = 2408^2 mod 5557. 2408^2 = 5,798,464.\n5557*1000 = 5,557,000. 5,798,464 - 5,557,000 = 241,464.\n5557*43 = 238,951. 241,464 - 238,951 = 2,513. So a8 = 2513.\nCheck 5557*43: 5557*40=222280, 5557*3=16671, total 238951. 241464-238951=2513. Good. a8 = 2513.\n\na9 = 2513^2 mod 5557. 2513^2 = 6,315,169.\n5557*1000 = 5,557,000. 6,315,169 - 5,557,000 = 758,169.\n5557*136 = 755,752. 758,169 - 755,752 = 2,417. So a9 = 2417.\nCheck 5557*136: 5557*100=555700, 5557*36=200052, total 755752. 758169-755752=2417. Good. a9 = 2417.\n\na10 = 2417^2 mod 5557. 2417^2 = 5,841,889.\n5557*1000 = 5,557,000. 5,841,889 - 5,557,000 = 284,889.\n5557*51 = 283,407. 284,889 - 283,407 = 1,482. So a10 = 1482.\nCheck 5557*51: 5557*50=277850, +5557=283407. 284889-283407=1482. Good. a10 = 1482.\n\na11 = 1482^2 mod 5557. 1482^2 = 2,196,324.\n5557*395 = 2,194,015. Hmm let me compute. 5557*400 = 2,222,800. Too big. 5557*395 = 5557*400 - 5557*5 = 2,222,800 - 27,785 = 2,195,015. 2,196,324 - 2,195,015 = 1,309. So a11 = 1309.\nCheck: 5557*395 = 2,195,015. 2,196,324 - 2,195,015 = 1,309. Good. a11 = 1309.\n\nSo the squaring table (7^(2^k) mod 5557):\nk=0: 7\nk=1: 49\nk=2: 2401\nk=3: 2192\nk=4: 3616\nk=5: 5392\nk=6: 4997\nk=7: 2408\nk=8: 2513\nk=9: 2417\nk=10: 1482\nk=11: 1309\n\nNow 2876 = 2^11 + 2^9 + 2^8 + 2^5 + 2^4 + 2^3 + 2^2. So I multiply a11 * a9 * a8 * a5 * a4 * a3 * a2 mod 5557.\n\nThat is: 1309 * 2417 * 2513 * 5392 * 3616 * 2192 * 2401 mod 5557.\n\nLet me multiply step by step, reducing mod 5557 each time.\n\nStart r = 1.\n\nMultiply by a11 = 1309: r = 1309.\n\nMultiply by a9 = 2417: r = 1309 * 2417 mod 5557.\n1309 * 2417 = ? 1309*2400 = 3,141,600. 1309*17 = 22,253. Total 3,163,853.\n5557*569 = ? 5557*500=2,778,500. 5557*69=383,433. Total 3,161,933. 3,163,853 - 3,161,933 = 1,920. So r = 1920.\nCheck 5557*69: 5557*70=388990, -5557=383433. Yes. 2778500+383433=3161933. 3163853-3161933=1920. Good. r = 1920.\n\nMultiply by a8 = 2513: r = 1920 * 2513 mod 5557.\n1920*2513 = 1920*2500 + 1920*13 = 4,800,000 + 24,960 = 4,824,960.\n5557*868 = ? 5557*800=4,445,600. 5557*68=377,876. Total 4,823,476. 4,824,960 - 4,823,476 = 1,484. So r = 1484.\nCheck 5557*68: 5557*60=333420, 5557*8=44456, total 377876. 4445600+377876=4823476. 4824960-4823476=1484. Good. r = 1484.\n\nMultiply by a5 = 5392: r = 1484 * 5392 mod 5557.\nNote 5392 ≡ -165. So r = 1484 * (-165) mod 5557 = -244,860 mod 5557.\n244,860 mod 5557: 5557*44 = 244,508. 244,860 - 244,508 = 352. So -244,860 ≡ -352 ≡ 5557-352 = 5205 mod 5557. So r = 5205.\nLet me double-check 1484*5392 directly: 1484*5392 = 1484*5000 + 1484*392 = 7,420,000 + 581,728 = 8,001,728. 5557*1440 = 8,002,080. Hmm that's slightly more. 5557*1439 = 8,002,080 - 5,557 = 7,996,523. 8,001,728 - 7,996,523 = 5,205. So r = 5205. \nWait, let me recompute 1484*392: 1484*400 = 593,600; 1484*8 = 11,872; 593,600 - 11,872 = 581,728. Yes. 7,420,000 + 581,728 = 8,001,728. \n5557*1440: 5557*1000=5,557,000; 5557*400=2,222,800; 5557*40=222,280. 5,557,000+2,222,800+222,280=8,002,080. Yes that's more than 8,001,728. So 1440 too big. 5557*1439 = 8,002,080-5,557 = 7,996,523. 8,001,728-7,996,523 = 5,205. r = 5205. Consistent with the -165 trick. Good. r = 5205.\n\nMultiply by a4 = 3616: r = 5205 * 3616 mod 5557.\nNote 5205 = 5557 - 352, so 5205 ≡ -352. r = -352 * 3616 mod 5557 = -1,272,832 mod 5557.\n1,272,832 mod 5557: 5557*229 = ? 5557*200=1,111,400. 5557*29=161,153. Total 1,272,553. 1,272,832 - 1,272,553 = 279. So -1,272,832 ≡ -279 ≡ 5557-279 = 5278 mod 5557. So r = 5278.\nLet me verify 5205*3616 directly: 5205*3616 = 5205*3600 + 5205*16 = 18,738,000 + 83,280 = 18,821,280. \n5557*3387 = ? This is getting big. Let me use the -352 result. -352*3616: 3616*352 = 3616*300 + 3616*52 = 1,084,800 + 188,032 = 1,272,832. Yes. 1,272,832 mod 5557 = 279 (since 5557*229=1,272,553, remainder 279). So -1,272,832 mod 5557 = 5557-279 = 5278. r = 5278.\nCheck 5557*229: 5557*229. 5557*200=1,111,400. 5557*29: 5557*30=166,710, -5557=161,153. 1,111,400+161,153=1,272,553. 1,272,832-1,272,553=279. Good. r = 5278.\n\nMultiply by a3 = 2192: r = 5278 * 2192 mod 5557.\nNote 5278 = 5557 - 279, so 5278 ≡ -279. r = -279 * 2192 mod 5557 = -611,568 mod 5557.\n611,568 mod 5557: 5557*110 = 611,270. 611,568 - 611,270 = 298. So -611,568 ≡ -298 ≡ 5557-298 = 5259 mod 5557. So r = 5259.\nCheck 279*2192: 279*2192 = 279*2000 + 279*192 = 558,000 + 53,568 = 611,568. Yes. 5557*110 = 611,270. 611,568-611,270 = 298. So -611,568 mod 5557 = 5557-298 = 5259. r = 5259.\n\nMultiply by a2 = 2401: r = 5259 * 2401 mod 5557.\nNote 5259 = 5557 - 298, so 5259 ≡ -298. r = -298 * 2401 mod 5557 = -715,498 mod 5557.\n715,498 mod 5557: 5557*128 = 711,296. 715,498 - 711,296 = 4,202. So -715,498 ≡ -4202 ≡ 5557-4202 = 1355 mod 5557. So r = 1355.\nCheck 298*2401: 298*2401 = 298*2400 + 298 = 715,200 + 298 = 715,498. Yes. 5557*128: 5557*100=555,700; 5557*28=155,596; total 711,296. 715,498-711,296=4,202. -4202 mod 5557 = 5557-4202 = 1355. r = 1355.\n\nSo the result should be 1355.\n\nWait, let me double-check the bit decomposition of 2876 and that I'm multiplying the right set of a_k.\n\n2876 = 2048 + 512 + 256 + 32 + 16 + 8 + 4\n= 2^11 + 2^9 + 2^8 + 2^5 + 2^4 + 2^3 + 2^2.\n\nSo exponents k = 11, 9, 8, 5, 4, 3, 2. Yes, that's a11, a9, a8, a5, a4, a3, a2. Correct.\n\nAnd I used Fermat: 8432 mod 5556 = 2876. Let me re-verify: 5556 + 2876 = 8432. Yes! 5556+2876 = 8432. Good.\n\nSo 7^8432 ≡ 7^2876 mod 5557 (since gcd(7,5557)=1 and 5557 prime, Fermat applies).\n\nResult = 1355.\n\nHmm, let me double check by re-doing the multiplication chain once more carefully, since a single arithmetic slip would invalidate it.\n\nSquaring table recap (each = prev^2 mod 5557):\na0 = 7\na1 = 49 ✓ (7^2)\na2 = 2401 ✓ (49^2 = 2401)\na3 = 2192: 2401^2 = 5,764,801. 5557*1037 = ? 5557*1000=5,557,000; 5557*37=205,609; total 5,762,609. Hmm wait, that doesn't match. Let me recompute. Earlier I said 5557*1000=5,557,000, remainder 207,801, then 5557*37=205,609, remainder 2,192. So 5557*1037 = 5,557,000+205,609 = 5,762,609. 5,764,801 - 5,762,609 = 2,192. ✓ a3=2192. Good. (I had written 5557*1037 implicitly via the two-step; consistent.)\n\na4 = 3616: 2192^2 = 4,804,864. 5557*864 = 4,801,248. Remainder 3,616. ✓\nLet me verify 2192^2: 2192^2 = (2200-8)^2 = 4,840,000 - 35,200 + 64 = 4,804,864. ✓. 5557*864: 5557*864, 5557*800=4,445,600, 5557*64=355,648, total 4,801,248. 4,804,864-4,801,248=3,616. ✓\n\na5 = 5392: 3616^2 = 13,075,456. 5557*2352 = 13,070,064. Remainder 5,392. ✓\n3616^2 = (3600+16)^2 = 12,960,000 + 115,200 + 256 = 13,075,456. ✓. 5557*2352: 5557*2000=11,114,000, 5557*352=1,956,064, total 13,070,064. 13,075,456-13,070,064=5,392. ✓\n\na6 = 4997: 5392^2 mod 5557. 5392 ≡ -165. (-165)^2=27,225. 5557*4=22,228. 27,225-22,228=4,997. ✓\n\na7 = 2408: 4997^2 mod 5557. 4997 ≡ -560. (-560)^2=313,600. 5557*56=311,192. 313,600-311,192=2,408. ✓\n\na8 = 2513: 2408^2 = 5,798,464. 5557*1043 = 5,557,000+238,951 = 5,795,951. Hmm, 5,798,464 - 5,795,951 = 2,513. ✓ \nWait, earlier I computed 5557*43 = 238,951 and 5557*1000=5,557,000, so 5557*1043 = 5,795,951, remainder 5,798,464-5,795,951 = 2,513. ✓. (Earlier I wrote 241,464 as the remainder after subtracting 5557*1000, which is 5,798,464-5,557,000=241,464, then 241,464-238,951=2,513. Consistent.) ✓\n\na9 = 2417: 2513^2 = 6,315,169. 5557*1136 = 5,557,000+755,752 = 6,312,752. 6,315,169-6,312,752 = 2,417. ✓\n2513^2 = (2500+13)^2 = 6,250,000 + 65,000 + 169 = 6,315,169. ✓. 5557*136=755,752. ✓.\n\na10 = 1482: 2417^2 = 5,841,889. 5557*1051 = 5,557,000+283,407 = 5,840,407. 5,841,889-5,840,407 = 1,482. ✓\n2417^2 = (2400+17)^2 = 5,760,000 + 81,600 + 289 = 5,841,889. ✓. 5557*51=283,407. ✓.\n\na11 = 1309: 1482^2 = 2,196,324. 5557*395 = 2,195,015. 2,196,324-2,195,015 = 1,309. ✓\n1482^2 = (1500-18)^2 = 2,250,000 - 54,000 + 324 = 2,196,324. ✓. 5557*395 = 5557*400 - 5557*5 = 2,222,800-27,785 = 2,195,015. ✓.\n\nGood, squaring table confirmed.\n\nNow the product: a11 * a9 * a8 * a5 * a4 * a3 * a2 mod 5557\n= 1309 * 2417 * 2513 * 5392 * 3616 * 2192 * 2401 mod 5557.\n\nStep 1: 1309 * 2417 mod 5557.\n1309*2417. Let me recompute. 1309*2417 = 1309*(2400+17) = 1309*2400 + 1309*17.\n1309*2400 = 1309*24*100 = (1309*24)*100. 1309*24 = 1309*20 + 1309*4 = 26,180 + 5,236 = 31,416. *100 = 3,141,600.\n1309*17 = 1309*10 + 1309*7 = 13,090 + 9,163 = 22,253.\nTotal = 3,141,600 + 22,253 = 3,163,853. ✓\n5557*569: 5557*500=2,778,500; 5557*69 = 5557*70 - 5557 = 388,990 - 5,557 = 383,433. Total 3,161,933. 3,163,853-3,161,933 = 1,920. ✓ r=1920.\n\nStep 2: 1920 * 2513 mod 5557.\n1920*2513 = 1920*2500 + 1920*13 = 4,800,000 + 24,960 = 4,824,960. ✓\n5557*868: 5557*800=4,445,600; 5557*68 = 5557*70 - 5557*2 = 388,990-11,114 = 377,876. Total 4,823,476. 4,824,960-4,823,476 = 1,484. ✓ r=1484.\n\nStep 3: 1484 * 5392 mod 5557.\nUsing 5392 ≡ -165: 1484 * (-165) = -244,860. \n1484*165 = 1484*100 + 1484*65 = 148,400 + 96,460 = 244,860. ✓ (1484*65 = 1484*60+1484*5 = 89,040+7,420 = 96,460. ✓)\n244,860 mod 5557: 5557*44 = 5557*40 + 5557*4 = 222,280+22,228 = 244,508. 244,860-244,508 = 352. So -244,860 ≡ -352 ≡ 5,205 mod 5557. ✓ r=5205.\n\nStep 4: 5205 * 3616 mod 5557.\nUsing 5205 ≡ -352: -352 * 3616 = -(352*3616). 352*3616 = 3616*352 = 3616*300 + 3616*52 = 1,084,800 + 188,032 = 1,272,832. \n3616*52 = 3616*50 + 3616*2 = 180,800+7,232 = 188,032. ✓. Total 1,272,832. ✓\n1,272,832 mod 5557: 5557*229 = 5557*200 + 5557*29 = 1,111,400 + 161,153 = 1,272,553. 1,272,832-1,272,553 = 279. So -1,272,832 ≡ -279 ≡ 5,278. ✓ r=5278.\n\nStep 5: 5278 * 2192 mod 5557.\nUsing 5278 ≡ -279: -279 * 2192 = -(279*2192). 279*2192 = 279*2000 + 279*192 = 558,000 + 53,568 = 611,568.\n279*192 = 279*200 - 279*8 = 55,800 - 2,232 = 53,568. ✓. Total 611,568. ✓\n611,568 mod 5557: 5557*110 = 611,270. 611,568-611,270 = 298. So -611,568 ≡ -298 ≡ 5,259. ✓ r=5259.\n\nStep 6: 5259 * 2401 mod 5557.\nUsing 5259 ≡ -298: -298 * 2401 = -(298*2401). 298*2401 = 298*2400 + 298 = 715,200 + 298 = 715,498. ✓\n715,498 mod 5557: 5557*128 = 5557*100 + 5557*28 = 555,700 + 155,596 = 711,296. 715,498-711,296 = 4,202. So -715,498 ≡ -4,202 ≡ 5557-4202 = 1,355. ✓ r=1355.\n\nSo the final remainder is 1355.\n\nLet me just sanity-check the Fermat reduction once more. 5557 is prime (verified by trial division up to 74). Fermat: 7^(5557-1) = 7^5556 ≡ 1 mod 5557, since gcd(7,5557)=1 (5557 not divisible by 7, confirmed: 7*793=5551). 8432 = 5556 + 2876, so 7^8432 = 7^5556 * 7^2876 ≡ 1 * 7^2876 ≡ 7^2876 mod 5557. ✓\n\n8432 - 5556 = 2876. ✓\n\nEverything checks. The answer is 1355.\n\nActually, let me also double-check that I don't have an off-by-one in the binary. 2876:\n2^11 = 2048. 2876-2048 = 828. 2^9 = 512. 828-512 = 316. 2^8 = 256. 316-256 = 60. 2^5 = 32. 60-32 = 28. 2^4 = 16. 28-16 = 12. 2^3 = 8. 12-8 = 4. 2^2 = 4. 4-4 = 0. ✓\nSo bits: 11, 9, 8, 5, 4, 3, 2. (Note 2^10=1024 not used, 2^7=128 not used, 2^6=64 not used, 2^1, 2^0 not used.) \n2048+512+256+32+16+8+4 = 2876. ✓\n\nGreat. Final answer: 1355.\n\nNow I'll write this up showing each squaring step briefly and state the final remainder on its own line. I won't use any tools."}},"_meta":{"totalTokens":2989,"eventId":"01a0b847-713d-7ca1-9b4a-ec79a1525fe0-4741","agentTimestampMs":1789798166008,"promptId":"b8af3c62-f681-4674-b537-b61dfdd2d28d","streamStartMs":1789798088063,"turnStartMs":1789798086281,"updateType":"AgentThoughtChunk","chunkId":4738}}}
